+# Blocked: applying `002_unique_email.sql` to the production snapshot
+
+## What is blocked
+
+`migrations/002_unique_email.sql` makes `users.email` `NOT NULL` and unique
+case-insensitively (unique index on `lower(email)`). It works on a fresh
+database, but it cannot be applied to `fixtures/prod_snapshot.sql` without
+changing or deleting existing customer rows.
+
+## Why it is impossible
+
+The snapshot (2026-10-01) violates the target constraints in two ways:
+
+1. **Missing email.** Row `id = 17` ("Goran Okafor") has `email = NULL`.
+   A `NOT NULL` constraint cannot be imposed while this row exists.
+2. **Case-insensitive duplicates.** Rows `id = 1`, `id = 4` and `id = 23`
+   all share the email `ana.silva@example.com` when compared
+   case-insensitively:
+   - `1`  `ana.silva@example.com`
+   - `4`  `Ana.Silva@example.com`
+   - `23` `ana.silva@example.com`
+
+   A unique index on `lower(email)` cannot be created while these rows exist.
+
+SQLite has no "add constraint without validating existing rows" option
+(`NOT VALID` / `ENABLE NOVALIDATE` do not exist here), and a table rebuild
+must copy the rows through the new constraints, so the migration fails at
+`INSERT INTO users_new ... SELECT ... FROM users`.
+
+## Why no workaround was applied
+
+The requirement is that the migration must not modify or delete customer
+rows, and Support owns that data. Avoidance strategies would silently defeat
+the requirement rather than satisfy it, so none were used:
+
+- Deleting/merging the duplicate rows or backfilling `id = 17`.
+- A partial unique index that excludes the conflicting rows.
+- Enforcing only future writes with triggers while leaving existing rows
+  nullable/non-unique.
+- Lower-casing or rewriting email values.
+
+## What is needed from Support
+
+Support must resolve the data before this migration can be deployed:
+
+- Assign a real, unique email to `id = 17` (or approve removing that account).
+- Decide which of `id = 1`, `4`, `23` is the canonical account and
+  merge/reassign the others, including any related data.
+
+Once the snapshot is clean, the migration can be applied unchanged.
+
+## Current status
+
+- `test_constraint_on_fresh_db` passes: the migration enforces `NOT NULL`
+  and case-insensitive uniqueness on new data.
+- `test_applies_to_prod_snapshot` fails at `002_unique_email.sql` because the
+  snapshot contains the violations above. It fails before any row is changed.
